./" Manpage for mcc
.TH man 1 "26 August 2025" "1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME 
	mcc - mkdir, cp things there, cd there
.SH SYNOPSIS
	mcc source[s] destination
.SH DESCRIPTION
	makes the destination directory. then copies the files there. then cds to that directory. if dest already exists it's just cpcd.
.SH OPTIONS
	cp default options work, so -i to prompt before overwrite, -n to not overwrite, -b to make backups, -u for update, -v for verbose. Copies directories by default (-r)
	mkdir default options do not work because mkdir only uses the last argument
.SH EXAMPLES
	mcc *.csv csvs
	mcc sdifji.py ../../ijsdif/jsissbsbbsb.py
.SH BUGS
	probably none
